  "name": "GROWTH HORMONE STIMULATION TEST - CLONIDIN",
  "code": "1763",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Normal Levels Of growth hormone are as below:</p>\n<table style=\"width: 94.9933%; height: 253.783px;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" data-cke-table-faked-selection-table=\"\">\n<tbody>\n<tr style=\"height: 24px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 46.2279%;\"><strong>Reference Group</strong></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 53.6244%;\"><strong>Reference Range in</strong><br><strong>ng/mL</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 20.3993px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 46.2279%;\"><strong>0-7 years</strong>&nbsp;</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 53.6244%;\">1.0-13.6</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 20.3993px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 46.2279%;\"><strong>8-11 years</strong>&nbsp;</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 53.6244%;\">1.0-16.4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 20.3993px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 46.2279%;\"><strong>12-15 years</strong>&nbsp;</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 53.6244%;\">1.0-14.4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 20.3993px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 46.2279%;\"><strong>16-19 years</strong></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 53.6244%;\">1.0-13.4</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 59.592px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 46.2279%;\"><strong>20-60 years</strong><br><strong>Males</strong><br><strong>Females</strong></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 53.6244%;\">&nbsp;<br>0.0-4.0<br>0.0-18.0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 88.5938px;\">\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 46.2279%;\"><strong>&gt;60 years</strong><br><strong>Males</strong><br><strong>Females</strong></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"width: 53.6244%;\">&nbsp;<br>1.0-9.0<br>1.0-16.0</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>1.&nbsp; Recommended stimulating agents are :</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div>&nbsp; a. Vigorous physical Exercise like running orcalisthenics performed for 20 minutes.</div>\n<div>&nbsp; b. Clonidine 300 ug maximum or 5 ug/Kg body weight orally.</div>\n<div>&nbsp; c. Insulin 0.10-0.15 U/Kg body weight IV.</div>\n<div><br>2&nbsp; &nbsp;To diagnose Growth hormone (GH) deficiency as a cause of growth retardation, at least 2 different provocative stimulants should be used on different days for confirmation.<br><br></div>\n<div>&nbsp; &nbsp; a. If post stimulation GH level is &gt; 7 ng/mL (If stimulating agent is Clonidine OR Exercise) / &gt; 10 ng/mL (If stimulating agent is Insulin),deficiency is unlikely</div>\n<div>&nbsp; &nbsp; b. An intermediate response (GH 3-6 ng/mL) should be considered suspect and further testing performed if clinically indicated</div>\n<div>&nbsp; &nbsp; c. Subnormal response is not diagnostic for GH deficiency and should be confirmed with another provocative test</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong>Clinical Use</strong></div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div>To demonstrate GH deficiency in cases of growth retardation, short stature and dwarfism</div>",
  "showInterpretation": false,
